#28506
"Central Bazaar, Southwest Corner"
"The shop to the south is dimly lit, so its contents currently remain a secret.
A sign above the shop flaps gently in the breeze, made of some strange scarlet
fur, and depicts a creature similar to a fox.  The shop to the west has several
glass windows in which a multitude of gems, jewelry, and other precious metals
are on display.  The pristine marble road continues to the north and east.  A
building that sits at the center of the bazaar rises above you to the northeast.
"
""
