#28507
"Central Bazaar, Southeast Corner"
"To the east is the source of the purple light, a glowing ball hanging above the
doorway to what looks to be a store of some sort.  There is no other marking to
indicate its contents.  The store to the south is more unassuming, with a
simple picture of a scroll etched into the marble on the right of the door.
The white marble road continues to the north and west.  A building that sits at
the center of the bazaar rises above you to the northwest.
"
""
