"Central Bazaar, Northeast Corner"
"The air is filled with the musty smell of animals and their unfortunate
leavings, making your eyes water slightly.  Neighs and whinnies are coming
from the east while barks, growls, and screeches fight for supremacy from the
north.  The splendid marble road continues to the south and west.  A building
that sits at the center of the bazaar looms to the southwest.
"
