#28519
"Outer Bazaar, West Side"
"To the west is the most lavish entrance to a building in the bazaar.  A bright
red carpet coats the half-dozen stairs that lead up to an ornate set of wooden
double-doors easily three stories high.  Immense stone columns flank the doors,
decorated with etchings of a multitude of races.  The smoothly-marbled road
continues to the north, where a massive domed building can be seen far in the
distance.  The road to the south brings you to the Cobalt district intersection.
"
"[DW] add acode to hear singing coming from the playhouse
"
