#28520
"Outer Bazaar, West Side"
"Vendors line the road, hawking their wares from various carts and stands. Most
of the vendors are selling useless tourist items, except for one stand that has
the scent of fresh, crisp vegetables and fruits emanating from it. There appear
to be no entrances to the buildings that lie to the east and west, at least
from here.  To the north is the Cobalt district intersection, while to the south
you can smell baking bread.
"
"Set vegetable seller here, as well as fruits and veggies stand
