#28522
"Outer Bazaar, West Side"
"The heavenly scent of freshly baked bread inundates the air around you.  The
store to the east, unlike most of the stores in the bazaar, has pure glass
walls, allowing you to see the variety of baked goods ready to be purchased.
Sweetmeat, bread, syrupy goodies, hard candy, fudge, and huge cookies decorate
the storefront.  The city road continues south toward a bend to the east, and
north toward a distant intersection.
"
"[DW] Smells of baking wafting from the east. (acode)
"
