#28524
"Outer Bazaar, Southwest Corner"
"To the south is an rustic wooden building, complete with a wooden sign labeled
'Inn' poking out over the road, quite out of place in a city filled with alien
materials and architecture.  A similarly decorated building lies to the east,
although much larger and with a mug of beer depicted on its sign.  The gleaming
white-marble road continues along the outer bazaar to the north and east.  The
distant scent of baked goods seem to come from both directions.
"
"[DW] Acode for raucous laughter coming from the west.
"
