#28525
"Outer Bazaar, South Side"
"The scent of freshly baked goods envelops you, drawing you toward the shop to
the north.  The store, unlike most of the stores in the bazaar, has pure glass
walls, allowing you to see the variety of baked goods ready to be purchased.
Sweetmeat, bread, syrupy goodies, hard candy, fudge, and huge cookies lure in
unwary travelers, changing their waistlines forever.  From the east drifts a
hint of spices, barely able to penetrate the wall of scents built by the
northern bakery.  To the west is a northern curve in the wide road that will
invariably lead to more shops.  The southern building looks like stables,
although you can't smell or hear anything coming from it.
"
"[DW] Smells of baking wafting from the north. (acode)
"
