#28536
"Outer Bazaar, East Side"
"The Bank of Val'Abun lies to the east, its name printed in many languages on
several signs affixed to the outside walls.  A carefully attended flower garden
surrounds the bank, filling the air with pleasant fragrances.  The wide, white
marbled road continues south toward the Emerald district intersection.  Long
shadows reach toward you from the north, although they seem to be unable to
penetrate far beyond its source: a large, black-marbled temple.  A glimpse of
sandy gold can be seen even farther to the north.
"
