#28537
"Outer Bazaar, East Side"
"The foreboding temple to the east is made entirely of an eerily black, seamless
marble that seems to absorb all ambient light around it.  The statue of a
unicorn in full gallop rises above the second floor's parapet, made of even
blacker material than the temple itself, although that does not seem rationally
possible.  Incredibly out of place is the smell of leather and oil coming from
a rustic shop to the west.  The subdued marble road continues south along the
outer bazaar ring, as well as north toward a sand-colored temple.
"
