sun on the apex of a church's steeple.  There is a sizable gap between the
church to the north and west and the temple to the northeast, filled by an
impeccably tended garden filled with strange, but colorful vegetation.  There
is a dusky, leathery smell in the air, and it seems to be coming from the shop
to the south.  Strangely out of place among the churches and temples of the
religious, the shop's sign depicts a saddle and horseshoe.
