Easily thirty feet high and as wide as a building, it still only takes up a
small section of the white-marbled road.  The water that filters down the
fountain's six levels is is pure and clear.  In the distance to the west you
can see a large set of cobalt-blue gates blocking the road.  The eastern road
takes you toward the bazaar's center, while the road to the north and south
continues along the outer bazaar ring.
