#28591
"Crimson District Crossroads"
"A @efountain@n unlike any you have seen before lies in the center of this
intersection.  It is made out of marble the color of human blood, but that is
the most mundane effect of it.  There are at least a dozen basins jutting out
at odd angles and heights, no rhyme or reason evident in its construction.  The
water in the fountain flows at gravity-defying angles; in some cases it even
flows upward.  Looking northward you can see a set of crimson gates in the
distance.  The marbled road south leads you toward the center of the bazaar,
while the road running east and west continue along the outer bazaar ring.
"
""
